<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2473" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμο-ρροΐς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ΐδος,
				ἡ</span>, mostly in pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμορροΐδες</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλέβες</span>) veins <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>liable to discharge blood</i>, esp. <i>haemorrhoids,
				piles</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				3.30
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> kind of
				<i>shell-fish</i>, perh. <i>Aporrhais pes-pelicani</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				530a19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> female of 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμόρροος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				20.210
			</span></i>; poet., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμοροΐς θήλεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					315
				</span></i>
			.</div>
